Consider the following contract:

interface Account {
  readonly id: string;
  nickname?: string;
}

With strictNullChecks enabled, what happens when code tries to reassign account.id = 'new-id' and accesses account.nickname?

A developer creates an object matching an interface with a readonly array property:

interface TagList {
  readonly tags: string[];
}
const list: TagList = { tags: ['typescript'] };

What does TypeScript allow or forbid when manipulating list?
